<main id="main">
<section class="ihero"><div class="ihero-text"><div class="ihero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ</span></nav><p class="kicker">Answers</p><h1>Alaska Insurance Appraisal FAQ, Grouped by Topic</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers to the questions we hear most: the basics, costs and timing, Alaska-specific rules and how we work.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line light" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div></div></div><figure class="ihero-photo"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-laptop.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 100vw, 55vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="FAQ topics"><p class="toc-h">Topics</p><ul><li><a href="#t0">The basics</a></li><li><a href="#t1">Costs and timing</a></li><li><a href="#t2">Alaska-specific questions</a></li><li><a href="#t3">Working with us</a></li></ul></nav><h2 id="t0">The basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A process in most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side appoints an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an award signed by two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>They are similar in that a neutral decides, but appraisal is usually limited to the amount of loss and tends to be less formal. Alaska courts and policy language determine how it works in a given case.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can invoke appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Either the policyholder or the insurer, under the terms of the policy. A written demand is usually required.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does my Alaska policy have an appraisal clause?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Most homeowner, condo, landlord and commercial property policies do. Look in the conditions section for a paragraph titled Appraisal.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t1">Costs and timing</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does appraisal cost?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Each side pays its own appraiser, and the umpire's fee is usually split. Total cost depends on the size and complexity of the claim and, in Alaska, on travel to the property.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does it take?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often two to three months for a simple residential claim after appraisers are named. Larger, remote or umpire-heavy claims can take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>When is the gap too small for appraisal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>If the costs would absorb most of the expected increase, a documented supplement request is often better. Our gap and fee estimator helps you check.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I invoke appraisal after accepting a payment?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often yes, depending on the policy and deadlines. Accepting a partial payment does not necessarily close a claim, but read any release carefully.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t2">Alaska-specific questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance in Alaska?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Alaska Division of Insurance, part of the Department of Commerce, Community, and Economic Development. It handles consumer complaints and licenses insurers and adjusters.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Alaska have a FAIR plan or a state wind pool?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Alaska does not operate a FAIR plan or a wind pool. Owners who cannot find standard coverage may turn to the surplus lines market.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does my homeowner policy cover earthquakes?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually not. Earthquake coverage is generally added by endorsement or separate policy and often carries a percentage deductible.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is flood covered?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Surface flooding, storm surge and glacial outburst flooding are typically excluded from homeowner policies and insured separately, for example through the National Flood Insurance Program.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you work on properties off the road system?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Remote properties need travel planning, and repair estimates should account for freight, travel and seasonal access.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="t3">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. We provide appraisal, estimating and umpire services. We do not negotiate claims outside appraisal and we do not give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you be my appraiser and the umpire?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. We serve in one role per claim and disclose any prior involvement.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I send for a free review?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Your declarations page, the carrier's full estimate, photos and any contractor estimates.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-stick"><div class="side-box call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through</h2><p>Free first conversation. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn gold block" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 8am–6pm Alaska Time</small></div><div class="side-box"><h2 class="side-h">Learn</h2><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-clause-process/">Appraisal process</a></li><li><a href="/alaska-appraisal-faq/" aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-claim-glossary/">Claim glossary</a></li><li><a href="/alaska-claim-guides/">Claim guides</a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-in rv"><div><p class="cta-h">Didn’t see your question?</p><p>Call or email and we’ll talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line light" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
